 $32.85 + $4.50 = $37.35\n- RDS primary: 730 × $0.068 × 2 (Multi-AZ) = $99.20\n- RDS storage: 20 × $0.115 × 2 (Multi-AZ) = $4.60\n- S3: 50 × $0.023 = $1.15\n- CloudFront data: 2000 × $0.085 = $170\n- CloudFront requests: 4000 × $0.01 = $40\n- Total: $30.37 + $16.43 + $11.68 + $37.35 + $99.20 + $4.60 + $1.15 + $170 + $40 = $410.78\n\nActual proposed cost: $410.78, well under the $750 budget (N5).\n\nWell-Architected alignment: Operational Excellence (7-day automated backups, PITR, Multi-AZ failover enabled, ASG for elastic scaling); Security (private compute subnets, NAT egress, ALB as public entry point); Reliability (N2–N3 fully met: 2 AZs, minimum 2 instances, Multi-AZ database with automatic failover and 7-day retention); Performance Efficiency (t3.small right-sized for 750 req/sec, CloudFront cache reduces origin load by 50%); Cost Optimization (stayed well under budget at $410.78, no over-provisioning, no unnecessary read replicas).",
